Everything `blockedGuestEntry` needs from `item` — guest authorship and the `pr_approved`/`ai_validating` labels — is already in the list item, so filtering **before** probing (skip machine PRs and unapproved/unarmed PRs) would cut the per-tick `prStatus` fan-out down to the handful of armed guests instead of one call per open PR per tick (list-probed PRs ride the 60s ioCache; the rest are fresh `gh` calls on the summary path).

